{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1307773-how-does-arcing-interact-with-cover","id":1307773,"title":"How Does Arcing Interact With Cover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-25T09:18:24-07:00","id":1307773,"title":"How Does Arcing Interact With Cover","content":"So I'm getting ready to run a Scion game, and two characters have a weapon with the Arcing Tag. Arcing ignores Light Cover and treats Heavy Cover as Light Cover. At first, I figured Cover must increase the difficulty to hit someone. However, when I went to read about how Cover works, I realized it works very much like Hard Armor where it absorbs damage. Light Cover absorbs 4 damage and Heavy Cover absorbs 10 damage before they are destroyed.<br /> <br /> This has some weird interactions with Arcing. Since Cover is destroyed when they reach 0 HP, and Arcing treats Heavy Cover as Light Cover, does that mean arcing destroys the Heavy Cover with only 4 damage instead of 10? I'm assuming it doesn't because other Bandmates without arcing might be shooting at the cover as well. So instead, does the Arcing only have to get through 4 HP of Heavy Cover before being able to hit while everyone else still has to deal with the other 6 HP? That's the interaction I'd have to assume, though that makes Arcing feel incredibly powerful compared to some other tags, as it's essentially ignoring 6 HP of Heavy Cover, which is kind of like ignoring 6 HP of the enemies behind it while everyone else slowly plinks away at the rest of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T09:23:03-07:00","id":1307774,"title":"","content":"I forgot to also ask: Are you still hitting versus the enemies Defense? If so, are you able to still Stunt against them like &quot;Disarm&quot; if you can't even hit them for damage because of the Cover?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T10:43:06-07:00","id":1307800,"title":"","content":"To my best understanding:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vulcan7200</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1307773-how-does-arcing-interact-with-cover#post1307773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming it doesn't because other Bandmates without arcing might be shooting at the cover as well. So instead, does the Arcing only have to get through 4 HP of Heavy Cover before being able to hit while everyone else still has to deal with the other 6 HP?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my interpretation of it as well if there's a single target<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's the interaction I'd have to assume, though that makes Arcing feel incredibly powerful compared to some other tags, as it's essentially ignoring 6 HP of Heavy Cover, which is kind of like ignoring 6 HP of the enemies behind it while everyone else slowly plinks away at the rest of it. </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that enemies share cover, so the more targets, the less cover each gets. If three enemies are behind Heavy Cover, one gets 4 Hard Armor, and two get 3 Hard Armor each. Someone with Arcing blows through an individual's cover with 2 damage, but that means there's only 1 or 2 damage left after for everyone else to deal with per target.<br /> <br /> I mean, you're right it's kinda boring if it's to PCs on one target and the second PC is stuck with those 6 HP, but they could take advantage of the target being pinned down to move around the cover or something instead of trying to go through it. But I'm not sure it's that power.<br /> <br /> Of course, what will really mess you up your day? There's four levels of Cover in the Storypath base system. Not that it's hard to slot them into the Arcing rules, it's just really confusing they did that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vulcan7200</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1307773-how-does-arcing-interact-with-cover?p=1307774#post1307774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot to also ask: Are you still hitting versus the enemies Defense? If so, are you able to still Stunt against them like &quot;Disarm&quot; if you can't even hit them for damage because of the Cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, their Defense still applies.<br /> <br /> There's no reason you can't use other stunts besides damage by the rules. If they're not under Full Cover, and thus capable of being attacked, parts of them are visible. If they're shooting at you, you have a chance to shoot their gun even if their body's protect and so on. But like most stunts I'd reserve some veto power if it doesn't make any sense for one of be applied in the moment.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}